        "defense": null,
        "description": {
            "value": "<p>You conjure a razor-sharp shard of scrap metal and imbue it with spiritual echoes of Gorum's death before launching it at a foe. Make a spell attack roll against the target. The warshard deals @Damage[5d6[piercing]] damage and @Damage[5d6[spirit]] damage, depending on your ranged spell attack roll against the target's AC.</p><hr /><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target takes double damage and @Damage[(@item.rank)[persistent,spirit]] damage. As long as the target is taking this persistent spirit damage, it takes a –1 status penalty to its AC.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The target takes full damage.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The target takes the spirit damage, but not the piercing damage.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The target is unaffected.</p><hr /><p><strong>Heightened (+1)</strong> The piercing damage and initial spirit damage each increase by 1d6. The persistent spirit damage on a critical hit increases by 1.</p>"
